:\"Offer\",\"priceCurrency\":\"USD\",\"price\":1549.00,\"sku\":\"MH644LL/A\",\"shippingDetails\":{\"@type\":\"OfferShippingDetails\",\"shippingRate\":{\"@type\":\"MonetaryAmount\",\"value\":0,\"currency\":\"USD\"}},\"hasMerchantReturnPolicy\":{\"@type\":\"MerchantReturnPolicy\",\"applicableCountry\":\"US\",\"returnPolicyCategory\":\"https://schema.org/MerchantReturnFiniteReturnWindow\",\"merchantReturnDays\":14,\"returnMethod\":\"https://schema.org/ReturnByMail\",\"returnFees\":\"https://schema.org/FreeReturn\"}},{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"priceCurrency\":\"USD\",\"price\":1549.00,\"sku\":\"MH654LL/A\",\"shippingDetails\":{\"@type\":\"OfferShippingDetails\",\"shippingRate\":{\"@type\":\"MonetaryAmount\",\"value\":0,\"currency\":\"USD\"}},\"hasMerchantReturnPolicy\":{\"@type\":\"MerchantReturnPolicy\",\"applicableCountry\":\"US\",\"returnPolicyCategory\":\"https://schema.org/MerchantReturnFiniteReturnWindow\",\"merchantReturnDays\":14,\"returnMethod\":\"https://schema.org/ReturnByMail\",\"returnFees\":\"https://schema.org/FreeReturn\"}},{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"priceCurrency\":\"USD\",\"price\":1049.00,\"sku\":\"MH5U4LL/A\",\"shippingDetails\":{\"@type\":\"OfferShippingDetails\",\"shippingRate\":{\"@type\":\"MonetaryAmount\",\"value\":0,\"currency\":\"USD\"}},\"hasMerchantReturnPolicy\":{\"@type\":\"MerchantReturnPolicy\",\"applicableCountry\":\"US\",\"returnPolicyCategory\":\"https://schema.org/MerchantReturnFiniteReturnWindow\",\"merchantReturnDays\":14,\"returnMethod\":\"https://schema.org/ReturnByMail\",\"returnFees\":\"https://schema.org/FreeReturn\"}},{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"priceCurrency\":\"USD\",\"price\":1399.00,\"sku\":\"MH9Q4LL/A\",\"shippingDetails\":{"},{"title":"iPad Air (1st generation)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IPad_Air_(1st_generation)","snippet":"Model iPad Air iPad Air 2 iPad Air (3rd generation) iPad Air (4th generation) iPad Air (5th generation) iPad Air (6th generation) iPad Air (7th generation) iPad Air (8th generation)\nOS Initial iOS 7.0.3 iOS 8.1 iOS 12.1.4 iPad OS 14.1 iPadOS 15.4 iPadOS 17.5 iPadOS 18.3.1 iPadOS 26.3.1\nOS Highest supported iOS 12.5.8…","date":"2026-08-09T00:30:12.000Z","content":"Model iPad Air iPad Air 2 iPad Air (3rd generation) iPad Air (4th generation) iPad Air (5th generation) iPad Air (6th generation) iPad Air (7th generation) iPad Air (8th generation)\nOS Initial iOS 7.0.3 iOS 8.1 iOS 12.1.4 iPad OS 14.1 iPadOS 15.4 iPadOS 17.5 iPadOS 18.3.1 iPadOS 26.3.1\nOS Highest supported iOS 12.5.8 [ 31 ] iPadOS 15.8.3 iPadOS 26.6\nModel number A1474 (Wi-Fi) A1475 (Wi-Fi + Cellular) A1476 (Wi-Fi + Cellular TD-LTE) A1566 (Wi-Fi) A1567 (Wi-Fi + Cellular) A2152 (Wi-Fi) A2123, A2153 (Wi-Fi + Cellular) A2154 (Wi-Fi + Cellular China) A2316 (Wi-Fi) A2324, A2072 (Wi-Fi + Cellular) A2325 (Wi-Fi + Cellular China) A2588 (Wi-Fi) A2589, A2591 (Wi-Fi + Cellular) 11-inch: A2902 (Wi-Fi) A2903 (Wi-Fi + Cellular) A2904 (Wi-Fi + Cellular China) 13-inch: A2898 (Wi-Fi) A2899 (Wi-Fi + Cellular) A2900 (Wi-Fi + Cellular China) 11-inch: A3266 (Wi-Fi) A3267 (Wi-Fi + Cellular) A3270 (Wi-Fi + Cellular China) 13-inch: A3268 (Wi-Fi) A3269 (Wi-Fi + Cellular) A3271 (Wi-Fi + Cellular China) 11-inch: A3459 (Wi-Fi) A3460 (Wi-Fi + Cellular) A3463 (Wi-Fi + Cellular China) 13-inch: A3461 (Wi-Fi) A3462 (Wi-Fi + Cellular) A3464 (Wi-Fi + Cellular China)\nModel identifier(s) iPad4,1 (Wi-Fi) iPad4,2 (Wi-Fi + Cellular) iPad4,3 (Wi-Fi + Cellular TD-LTE) iPad5,3 (Wi-Fi) iPad5,4 (Wi-Fi + Cellular) iPad11,3 (Wi-Fi) iPad11,4 (Wi-Fi + Cellular (All regions)) iPad13,1 (Wi-Fi) iPad13,2 (Wi-Fi + Cellular (All regions)) iPad13,3 (Wi-Fi) iPad13,4 (Wi-Fi + Cellular (All regions)) iPad14,8 (Wi-Fi) iPad14,9 (Wi-Fi + Cellular (All regions)) iPad14,10 (Wi-Fi) iPad14,11 (Wi-Fi + Cellular (All regions)) iPad15,3 (Wi-Fi) iPad15,4 (Wi-Fi + Cellular (All regions)) iPad15,5 (Wi-Fi) iPad15,6 (Wi-Fi + Cellular (All regions)) iPad16,3 (Wi-Fi) iPad16,4 (Wi-Fi + Cellular (All regions)) iPad16,5 (Wi-Fi) iPad16,6 (Wi-Fi + Cellular (All regions))\nAnnouncement date October 22, 2013 October 16, 2014 March 18, 2019 September 15, 2020 March 8, 2022 May 7, 2024 March 4, 2025 March 2, 2026\nRelease date November 1, 2013 16, 64, 128 GB: October 22, 2014 32 GB and 128 GB re-released: September 7, 2016 March 18, 2019 October 23, 2020 March 18, 2022 May 15, 2024 March 12, 2025 March 11, 2026\nDiscontinued 64, 128 GB: October 16, 2014 16, 32 GB: March 21, 2016 128 GB: March 21, 2016 16, 64 GB: September 7, 2016 32, 128 GB (re-released): March 21, 2017 September 15, 2020 March 8, 2022 May 7, 2024 March 4, 2025 March 2, 2026 Current\nLaunch price Wi-Fi models 16 GB $499 32 GB $599 64 GB $699 128 GB $799 Wi-Fi + Cellular models 16 GB $629 32 GB $729 64 GB $829 128 GB $929 Wi-Fi models 16 GB $499 64 GB $599 128 GB $699 Wi-Fi + Cellular models 16 GB $629 64 GB $729 128 GB $829 Wi-Fi models 64 GB $499 256 GB $649 Wi-Fi + Cellular models 64 GB $629 256 GB $779 Wi-Fi models 64 GB $599 256 GB $749 Wi-Fi + Cellular models 64 GB $729 256 GB $879 Wi-Fi models 64 GB $599 256 GB $749 Wi-Fi + Cellular models 64 GB $729 256 GB $879 Wi-Fi models 128 GB $599 256 GB $699 512 GB $899 1 TB $1099 Wi-Fi + Cellular models 128 GB $749 256 GB $849 512 GB $1049 1 TB $1249 Wi-Fi models 128 GB $799 256 GB $899 512 GB $1099 1 TB $1299 Wi-Fi + Cellular models 128 GB $949 256 GB $1049 512 GB $1249 1 TB $1449 Wi-Fi models 128 GB $599 256 GB $699 512 GB $899 1 TB $1099 Wi-Fi + Cellular models 128 GB $749 256 GB $849 512 GB $1049 1 TB $1249 Wi-Fi models 128 GB $799 256 GB $899 512 GB $1099 1 TB $1299 Wi-Fi + Cellular models 128 GB $949 256 GB $1049 512 GB $1249 1 TB $1449 Wi-Fi models 128 GB $599 256 GB $699 512 GB $899 1 TB $1099 Wi-Fi + Cellular models 128 GB $749 256 GB $849 512 GB $1049 1 TB $1249 Wi-Fi models 128 GB $799 256 GB $899 512 GB $1099 1 TB $1299 Wi-Fi + Cellular models 128 GB $949 256 GB $1049 512 GB $1249 1 TB $1449\nSoC Name Apple A7 Apple A8X Apple A12 Bionic Apple A14 Bionic Apple M1 Apple M2 Apple M3 Apple M4\nSoC Motion coprocessor Apple M7 Apple M8 Apple A12 Bionic Apple A14 Bionic Apple M1 Apple M2 Apple M3 Apple M4\nSoC CPU 1.4 GHz dual-core Apple Cyclone 1.5 GHz tri-core Apple Typhoon 2.49 GHz 6-core (Dual-core Vortex + quad-core Tempest) 3.10 GHz 6-core (Dual-core Firestorm + quad-core Icestorm) 3.20 GHz 8-core (quad-core Firestorm + quad-core Icestorm) 3.49 GHz (quad-core Avalanche) + 2.42 GHz (quad-core Blizzard) 4.05 GHz (quad-core performance) + 2.75 GHz (quad-core efficient) 4.10 Ghz (3 performance cores) + 2.75 Ghz (5 efficiency cores)\nSoC GPU Quad-core PowerVR G6430 Octa-core PowerVR GXA6850 Apple designed quad-core Apple designed octa-core Apple designed octa-core Apple designed nona-core Apple designed nona-core\nSoC Memory 1 GB LPDDR3 RAM 2 GB LPDDR3 RAM 3 GB LPDDR4X RAM 4 GB RAM 8 GB RAM 8 GB RAM 8 GB RAM 12 GB RAM\nStorage 16, 32, 64, or 128 GB 16, 64, or 128 GB 64 or 256 GB 128, 256, 512 GB or 1 TB","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","engines":["web"]},{"title":"iPad Air","url":"https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-air/","snippet":"Apple refreshed the iPad Air in March 2026 with two eighth-generation models, adding updated M4 chips, the C1X modem, and N1 networking chip to the lineup. The iPad Air continues to be available in 11-inch and 13-inch sizes, much like the iPad Pro, and there were no design changes in 2026. Priced starting at $749, the…","date":"2026-08-15T03:31:38.000Z","content":"Apple refreshed the iPad Air in March 2026 with two eighth-generation models, adding updated M4 chips, the C1X modem, and N1 networking chip to the lineup. The iPad Air continues to be available in 11-inch and 13-inch sizes, much like the iPad Pro, and there were no design changes in 2026. Priced starting at $749, the iPad Air is Apple's middle-of-the-road option, as it is more affordable than the $1,199+ iPad Pro but more expensive than the $449 11th-generation iPad.\nThe smaller iPad Air has an 11-inch edge-to-edge display with a 2360x1640 resolution, while the larger iPad Air has a 13-inch edge-to-edge display with a 2732x2048 resolution. The iPad Air is equipped with an LCD \"Liquid Retina\" display that is a step down from the OLED display in the iPad Pro. Compared to the iPad Pro, the iPad Air is thicker, heavier, and has thicker display bezels.\nThe iPad Air has an aluminum chassis that has flat sides and rounded edges that wrap around the fully laminated display. True Tone support is included for adjusting the display to match the ambient lighting, as is P3 wide color, 500 nits brightness for the 11-inch model and 600 nits for the 13-inch model, and 1.8 percent reflectivity. It does not feature ProMotion support.\nThe 2026 iPad Air comes in Space Gray, Purple, Blue, and Starlight, which are the same colors offered in 2025. The iPad Air includes a Touch ID sensor integrated into the top button rather than Face ID like the iPad Pro. Other than being built into the top button instead of a Home button, the Touch ID functionality is the same as other devices that have featured Touch ID.\nCompared to the 2025 model, there are no design changes or other internal updates except for the Apple-designed chips that are inside, like the M4 chip. The M4 chip is built on TSMC's N3E 3nm process, and it is more powerful and efficient than the prior-generation M3.\nThe M4 has an 8-core CPU and a 9-core GPU, and it is 30 percent faster than the M3 according to Apple. Memory bandwidth has increased to 120GB/s, and the iPad Air now comes with 12GB RAM, up from 8GB.\nThe 12-megapixel front-facing FaceTime camera supports Center Stage, and there is a 12-megapixel ƒ/1.8 rear camera. The iPad Air includes stereo speakers in landscape mode for wider stereo sound when watching video.\nCellular iPad Air models are compatible with 5G networks, but support is limited to the slower and more widespread sub-6GHz 5G networks with Apple's C1X modem. Storage continues to start at 128GB, but can be upgraded to as much as 1TB. Other features include Wi-Fi 7, Bluetooth 6, and Thread support thanks to the N1 networking chip.\nThe iPad Air has a USB-C port with up to 10Gbps data transfer along with support for connecting cameras for downloading images, hard drives, and external monitors. The iPad Air ships with a 20W USB-C adapter for charging purposes.\nLike the iPad Pro, the iPad Air supports the $129 Apple Pencil Pro and it works with a new Magic Keyboard for iPad Air. The Magic Keyboard attaches to the iPad Air magnetically, with the Smart Connector providing power and data with no need for Bluetooth.\nNote: See an error in this roundup or want to offer feedback? Send us an email here.","domain":"macrumors.com","engines":["web"]},{"title":"Apple iPad Air","url":"https://www.gsmarena.com/apple_ipad_air-5797.php","snippet":"Versions: Apple iPad Air Wi-Fi + Cellular (3G/LTE); Apple iPad Air Wi-Fi (Wi-Fi, w/o GPS)\n2G bands GSM 850 / 900 / 1800 / 1900\n3G bands HSDPA 850 / 900 / 1700(AWS) / 1900 / 2100\n4G bands 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 13, 17, 18, 19, 20, 25, 26\nSpeed HSPA 42.2/5.76 Mbps, LTE Cat3 100/50 Mbps, EV-DO Rev.A 3.1 Mbps - cellular mod…","date":"2026-08-08T04:01:10.000Z","content":"Versions: Apple iPad Air Wi-Fi + Cellular (3G/LTE); Apple iPad Air Wi-Fi (Wi-Fi, w/o GPS)\n2G bands GSM 850 / 900 / 1800 / 1900\n3G bands HSDPA 850 / 900 / 1700(AWS) / 1900 / 2100\n4G bands 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 13, 17, 18, 19, 20, 25, 26\nSpeed HSPA 42.2/5.76 Mbps, LTE Cat3 100/50 Mbps, EV-DO Rev.A 3.1 Mbps - cellular model only\nLaunch Announced 2013, October 22. Released 2013, November 01\nBody Dimensions 240 x 169.5 x 7.5 mm (9.45 x 6.67 x 0.30 in)","domain":"gsmarena.com","engines":["web"]},{"title":"Apple iPad Air 2024 release date, specs, & price now confirmed","url":"https://www.pcguide.com/tablet/apple-ipad-air-2024-release-date-specs-price/","snippet":"128GB (11-inch) $599 £599 $799\n256GB (11-inch) $699 £699 $949\n512GB (11-inch) $899 £899 $1,229\n1TB (11-inch) $1,099 £1,099 $1,509\n128GB (13-inch) $799 £799 $1,099\n256GB (13-inch) $899 £899 $1,249\n512GB (13-inch) $1,099 £1,099 $1,529\n1TB (13-inch) $1,299 £1,299 $1,809\nWhen it comes to the price tag, the new 11′′ model…","date":"2026-08-16T12:23:27.000Z","content":"128GB (11-inch) $599 £599 $799\n256GB (11-inch) $699 £699 $949\n512GB (11-inch) $899 £899 $1,229\n1TB (11-inch) $1,099 £1,099 $1,509\n128GB (13-inch) $799 £799 $1,099\n256GB (13-inch) $899 £899 $1,249\n512GB (13-inch) $1,099 £1,099 $1,529\n1TB (13-inch) $1,299 £1,299 $1,809\nWhen it comes to the price tag, the new 11′′ model has stayed true to that of the last-gen 11′′ iPad Air, with the 5th-gen model (10.9-inch) costing you $599/£599. However, there’s an expected price boost when it comes to the larger of the two models, and Apple has added on an extra $200 for the two inches of screen real estate, giving the 13′′ iPad Air a starting price of $799/£799.","domain":"pcguide.com","engines":["web"]},{"title":"iPad Air","url":"https://www.macrumors.com/guide/2022-ipad-air","snippet":"Apple's iPad Air is the middle-tier iPad starting at $749 in 11-inch and 13-inch size options.\nShould You Buy an iPad Air?\nThe iPad Air is Apple's mid-range tablet, featuring an M4 chip, Touch ID, two display sizes, Wi-Fi 7, and Apple Pencil support. Refreshed in March 2026, the iPad Air is mid-way through its product…","date":"2026-08-28T21:45:34.000Z","content":"Apple's iPad Air is the middle-tier iPad starting at $749 in 11-inch and 13-inch size options.\nShould You Buy an iPad Air?\nThe iPad Air is Apple's mid-range tablet, featuring an M4 chip, Touch ID, two display sizes, Wi-Fi 7, and Apple Pencil support. Refreshed in March 2026, the iPad Air is mid-way through its product cycle and it's still a good time to buy. We aren't expecting a new model until spring 2027 at the earliest.\nApple increased the price of the iPad Air by $150 in June 2026, and it now starts at $749 instead of $599. Apple is charging more for the iPad Air because the global memory shortage has driven up Apple's component costs.\nThe iPad Air is the sweet spot in Apple's iPad lineup, but for those who want a smaller tablet, there is the iPad mini, which still offers many of the iPad Air's capabilities in a more portable form factor. Users who are looking for a more affordable option should consider the 11th-generation iPad. Starting at $449, the iPad offers several iPad Air features, such as Touch ID and a Retina display, but at a lower price.\nOn the other hand, for iPad models with a more advanced display and improved performance, there is the iPad Pro. The iPad Pro takes the iPad Air's features to a new level, adding an OLED display, up to 16GB of memory, Face ID, ProMotion, an M5 chip, and more. It is aimed at professional users who need more power and higher-end display options.\nM4 iPad Air vs. M5 iPad Pro Buyer's Guide: 40+ Differences Compared\nIf you're planning to get an iPad Air or another iPad, make sure to check out our iPad deals guide, where we aggregate the best prices of the month.","domain":"macrumors.com","engines":["web"]},{"title":"Apple iPad Air & Mini","url":"https://www.umart.com.au/corporate/laptops-computers/apple/apple-ipad-air-mini-881","snippet":"Shop Apple iPad Air & Mini online today from our unbeatable range of Apple iPad - Buy Now, Pay Later + FREE pick-up & same day dispatch!","date":"2026-08-17T13:19:32.000Z","domain":"umart.com.au","engines":["web"]},{"title":"The iPad Air 2 is much faster than the iPhone 6 and the original iPad Air","url":"https://www.idownloadblog.com/2014/10/21/the-ipad-air-2-is-much-faster-than-the-iphone-6-and-the-original-ipad-air/","snippet":"The iPad Air 2 is much faster than the iPhone 6 and the original iPad Air\nNo big shocker at first glance. Of course the iPad Air 2, a device that’s just now landing into the hands of rabid fans, is faster than the year-old device that it’s intended to replace. Yes, the iPad Air 2 is faster, but it’s the way that it’s…","date":"2026-08-18T16:39:50.000Z","content":"The iPad Air 2 is much faster than the iPhone 6 and the original iPad Air\nNo big shocker at first glance. Of course the iPad Air 2, a device that’s just now landing into the hands of rabid fans, is faster than the year-old device that it’s intended to replace. Yes, the iPad Air 2 is faster, but it’s the way that it’s faster that is truly noteworthy.\nThe A8X processor that’s nestled deep within the confines of the iPad Air 2’s new slim and trim body is, for the first time in the history of iOS devices, a 1.5Ghz triple-core processor. The iPad Air 2 also features a healthy 2GB of RAM. Coincidentally, the 2GB of RAM is also a first for any iOS device.\nNeedless to say, the iPad Air 2 is a beast on paper, but it’s no mere paper tiger. This thing screams, and the first benchmarks posted on MacRumors comparing it to previous iOS devices are proving that point.","domain":"idownloadblog.com","engines":["web"]},{"title":"APPLE iPad AIR(2022)","url":"https://www.techyv.com/article-tag/apple-ipad-air2022/","snippet":"","date":"2026-08-16T08:43:56.000Z","domain":"techyv.com","engines":["web"]},{"title":"We tracked down 11 of the best iPad deals live for October Prime Day","url":"https://mashable.com/article/oct-prime-day-ipad-deals-2025","snippet":"Apple iPad Air, 11-inch (M3, WiFi, 128GB) — $449 $599(save $150) 🔥\nApple iPad Air, 11-inch (M3, WiFi + cellular, 128GB) — $599 $749(save $150) 🔥\nApple iPad Air, 13-inch (M3, WiFi, 128GB) — $649 $799(save $150) 🔥\nApple iPad Air, 13-inch (M3, WiFi + cellular, 128GB) — $866 $949(save $83) 🔥","date":"2026-09-23T14:20:53.000Z","domain":"mashable.com","engines":["web"]},{"title":"iPad Air, tableta e vitit","url":"https://lajmi.net/ipad-air-tableta-e-vitit/","snippet":"","date":"2026-08-14T18:58:45.000Z","domain":"lajmi.net","engines":["web"]},{"title":"Tuesday, October 22, 2013","url":"http://asiasingapore.blogspot.com/search/label/Apple%20Singapore","snippet":"Apple has announced its new iPad line of tablets. iPad Air, the 5th generation of iPad, will be equipped with new A7 processor and is just 450 gram. iPad Mini Retina Display, 2nd generation of iPad Mini, will be equipped with A7 processor and retina display.\niPad Air release date in Singapore, Hong Kong, China and Jap…","date":"2026-07-14T03:41:36.000Z","content":"Apple has announced its new iPad line of tablets. iPad Air, the 5th generation of iPad, will be equipped with new A7 processor and is just 450 gram. iPad Mini Retina Display, 2nd generation of iPad Mini, will be equipped with A7 processor and retina display.\niPad Air release date in Singapore, Hong Kong, China and Japan is November 1st 2013. Although Apple kept iPad as a pretty expensive tablet, expect long lines of queues for the new device and an overwhelming demand.\niPad Air Specifications and Prices 240 x 169.5 x 7.5 mm iPad Air will weight just 469 grams and come in silver, space gray and aluminum colors. 9.7 inch and 2,048 x 1,536 pixels screen will hide a 64-bit A7 processor behind and a battery powering the device for 10 hours on Wi-Fi. iPad Air still comes with 5 megapixels camera.\niPad Air prices for only Wi-Fi version are US $499 for 16 GB, US $599 for 32 GB, US $699 for 64 GB and US $799 for 128 GB models. For Wi-Fi plus cellular iPad Air prices are US $629 for 16 GB US $729 for 32 GB, US $829 for 64 GB and US $929 for 128 GB models.\niPad Mini 2 prices for only Wi-Fi version are US $399 for 16 GB, US $499 for 32 GB, US $599 for 64 GB and US $699 for 128 GB models. For Wi-Fi plus cellular iPad Air prices are US $529 for 16 GB US $629 for 32 GB, US $729 for 64 GB and US $829 for 128 GB models.","domain":"asiasingapore.blogspot.com","engines":["web"]},{"title":"Apple’s iPad Air","url":"https://variety.com/gallery/executech-speeding-up-the-screen-scene-with-apples-ipad-air-amazon-kindle-fire-hdx-more/","snippet":"apple.com | up to $929 with 128GB: Apple’s fifth-generation iPad slims down with the new iPad Air, weighing just 1 pound (down from the fourth generation’s 1.44 pounds) and measuring just 7.5 millimeters thick (vs. 9.4 mm). If that’s barely noticeable, the new A7 chip and M7 co-processor make it eight-times faster, an…","date":"2026-08-18T10:45:53.000Z","content":"apple.com | up to $929 with 128GB: Apple’s fifth-generation iPad slims down with the new iPad Air, weighing just 1 pound (down from the fourth generation’s 1.44 pounds) and measuring just 7.5 millimeters thick (vs. 9.4 mm). If that’s barely noticeable, the new A7 chip and M7 co-processor make it eight-times faster, and render graphics at twice the rate of the previous iPad. The same chip powers the iPhone 5S. A 5-megapixel iSight camera on the rear, and updated FaceTime HD camera, and dual microphones, may not be the dramatic updates the Apple faithful may have wanted. But at 10 hours of battery life, the 9.7-inch iPad Air is a device that packs enough of a punch to still make it the one to beat.","domain":"variety.com","engines":["web"]},{"title":"IPad","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IPad","snippet":"Since then, the iPad product line has been expanded to include the smaller iPad Mini, the lighter and thinner iPad Air , and the flagship iPad Pro models","date":"2026-10-08T19:04:06Z","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","engines":["web"]}],"images":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IPad_Air_(1st_generation)","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/IPad_Air.png/330px-IPad_Air.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","title":"IPad Air (1st generation)","source":"en.wikipedia.org","license":"source","credit":"Wikipedia"}],"knowledge":{"title":"IPad Air (1st generation)","extract":"The iPad Air is a tablet computer developed and marketed by Apple Inc. It was announced on October 22, 2013 and released on November 1, 2013. Part of the iPad line of tablet computers, the iPad Air features a thinner design than its predecessors, with similarities to the contemporaneous iPad Mini 2.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IPad_Air_(1st_generation)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/IPad_Air.png/330px-IPad_Air.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","description":"Tablet computer developed by Apple Inc. (2013–2016)"},"discussions":[{"title":"How do I take my iOS app from $1.5k/mth currently to $10k/mth?","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=2726801","points":2,"comments":4,"date":"2011-07-04T15:39:23Z"},{"title":"Ask HN: Moving balls to the wall on a fantastic idea?","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=1256736","points":22,"comments":16,"date":"2010-04-11T12:13:46Z"},{"title":"Ask HN: Apple North Carolina Data Center","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=1780503","points":1,"comments":1,"date":"2010-10-11T17:49:58Z"},{"title":"The End of the Road for the actual American pastime…TV","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4072034","points":2,"comments":1,"date":"2012-06-06T02:04:27Z"}],"engines":[{"name":"web","ok":false,"count":0,"ms":0,"error":"skipped"},{"name":"web","ok":true,"count":20,"ms":3759},{"name":"web","ok":true,"count":5,"ms":345}]}

